{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Feddry","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/feddry.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/feddry.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Feddry","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":15,"temp":0,"max":15,"details":""},"ac":{"value":16,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"(spoken and signed)"},"level":{"value":0},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Feddry are amphibious humanoids who protect themselves by wearing rocks. Feddry typically appear as several feathery tendrils emerging from a porous rock, contorting into an exaggerated human-like face with feathery gills, bulging eyes, and a nearly accurate humanoid body. A feddry in this form is positively abuzz with excitement.</p>\n<p>Feddry are best known for their simplistic views of the universe. To them, everything is either a feddry or a rock. Anything capable of movement or action, including air and water currents, is a feddry, while anything else is a rock. Rocks are meant to protect feddry. Many feddry engage in long, drawn-out debates over the nature of feddry and the use of rocks, making them quaint and befuddling conversationalists. Many feddry colonies can be found near coral reefs; though feddry can move farther inland, they prefer plankton-filled water for food.</p>\n<p>Feddry outside of their rock homes have malleable bodies, which are made of long, flexible tendrils wrapped in layers. Even so, most feddry can't be convinced to take on any form other than a small humanoid with two arms, two legs, and a head, with their home rock serving as the torso. When at rest or scared, a feddry often retreats into its personal rock.</p>\n<p>A feddry's rock serves as protective armor for most of its vitals; inside is a tangle of further tendrils, tubes, and bulges. Feddry have no concept of gender, and study has only determined that they have a plankton-like life stage before attaching to a proper rock.</p>\n<h2>A Rock By Any Other Name</h2>\n<p>Although feddry are considered simplistic by many, their society is more complex than it seems to outsiders. One well-known incident occurred when a feddry's pet rock insisted that it was a feddry. The claim nearly led to a schism in feddry society until one of them pointed out that since all feddry would one day become rocks, there was no reason a rock could not become a feddry.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 2.25/5/9 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), skill items (Crafting, Deception, Diplomacy, Lore [Rock], Society, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> charisma, constitution, dexterity, electricity, energy resistant (positive), strength, throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Aaron B. Bradford","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":0},"wis":{"mod":1},"cha":{"mod":3}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":6,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":6,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":9,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":3,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"crafting":{"base":3},"deception":{"base":5},"diplomacy":{"base":5},"society":{"base":3},"stealth":{"base":6}},"traits":{"value":["amphibious","feddry","humanoid"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/feddry.webp","items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Low-Light Vision","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.LowLightVision]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"low-light-vision","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.0.2","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1687478146903,"modifiedTime":1687478146903,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.fFu2sZz4KB01fVRc","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":nul